From c10bb5f39f44c6041552d86f10da568d4ffe1d1f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: isyourbrainfoss <isyourbrainfoss@proton.me>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 15:30:52 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] imsd: play early media, and local ringback when alerting has
 none

A 1xx only moved the call to ringing. Nothing opened RTP or played a
tone before 200 OK, so an outgoing VoLTE call was silent while the
other party was alerted.

Play a downlink-only media leg when this 1xx carries an audio answer
and backward early media is allowed (P-Early-Media sendrecv or
sendonly, else a non-precondition SDP). Otherwise play a local 425 Hz
tone, 1s on and 4s off, and stop it on answer or hangup. If that early
leg ends before the answer, fall back to the tone.
---
